### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SHORTLY API — VS Code REST Client Test Suite (v2)
### Usage:
###   1. Install "REST Client" extension by Huachao Mao
###   2. Open this file → click "Send Request" above each request
###   3. Run TOP-TO-BOTTOM on a fresh DB (run `node cleanup.js` first)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@apiVersion = v1
@contentType = application/json

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 1 — HEALTH & INFO
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1.1 Root endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 1.2 Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 1.3 API status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/status

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 2 — AUTH
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 2.1 Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Mohitt Test",
  "email": "mohitt-test@example.com",
  "password": "MySecurePass123!"
}

### 2.2 Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "mohitt-test@example.com",
  "password": "MySecurePass123!"
}

### 2.3 Extract tokens (from register or login — pick one)
@accessToken = {{register.response.body.data.access_token}}
@refreshToken = {{register.response.body.data.refresh_token}}
@apiKey = {{register.response.body.data.api_key}}

### 2.4 /me with Bearer token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2.5 /me with API key
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 2.6 Refresh tokens
# @name refreshResp
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 2.7 Wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "mohitt-test@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

### 2.8 Duplicate email (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "email": "mohitt-test@example.com",
  "password": "AnotherPass456!"
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 3 — URL CREATION
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 3.1 Create anonymous URL
# @name anonCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "long_url": "https://example.com/anonymous-test"
}

### 3.2 Create owned URL with custom alias
# @name authCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "long_url": "https://github.com/mohitt1213",
  "custom_alias": "mohitt-gh"
}

### 3.3 Create URL with expiration
# @name expCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "long_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com",
  "expires_at": "2027-12-31T23:59:59Z"
}

### 3.4 Invalid URL (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "long_url": "not-a-valid-url"
}

### 3.5 Reserved alias (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "long_url": "https://example.com",
  "custom_alias": "api"
}

### 3.6 Duplicate alias (expect 409) — run after 3.2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "long_url": "https://different.com",
  "custom_alias": "mohitt-gh"
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 4 — URL MANAGEMENT
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 4.1 List my URLs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.2 List without auth (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls

### 4.3 Public details (expect isOwner: false)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls/mohitt-gh

### 4.4 Owner details (expect isOwner: true)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls/mohitt-gh
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.5 Update expiration (owner)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls/mohitt-gh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "expires_at": "2027-06-30T23:59:59Z"
}

### 4.6 Update without auth (expect 401)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls/mohitt-gh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "expires_at": "2027-06-30T23:59:59Z"
}

### 4.7 Try to delete ANONYMOUS URL (expect 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls/{{anonCreate.response.body.data.short_code}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 5 — REDIRECT (uses LIVE URLs created above)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 5.1 Redirect OWNED custom alias → expect 302
GET {{baseUrl}}/mohitt-gh

### 5.2 Redirect ANONYMOUS URL → expect 302
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{anonCreate.response.body.data.short_code}}

### 5.3 Redirect EXPIRATION URL → expect 302
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{expCreate.response.body.data.short_code}}

### 5.4 Redirect NON-EXISTENT → expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/doesnotexist999xyz

### 5.5 Health still works → expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 6 — ANALYTICS (uses LIVE URLs)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 6.1 Analytics for OWNED URL
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/analytics/mohitt-gh?days=30

### 6.2 Analytics for EXPIRATION URL
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/analytics/{{expCreate.response.body.data.short_code}}?days=7

### 6.3 Analytics for NON-EXISTENT (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/analytics/doesnotexist999xyz

### 6.4 Manual flush (owner)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/analytics/flush
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 7 — CLEANUP (Delete owned URL — run AFTER redirects)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 7.1 Delete OWNED URL
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls/mohitt-gh
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 7.2 Verify deleted (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/urls/mohitt-gh

### 7.3 Redirect to deleted (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/mohitt-gh

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SECTION 8 — LOGOUT
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 8.1 Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 8.2 Try refresh after logout (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### NOTES
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###
### 🎯 CORRECT TEST ORDER:
###   1. Run `node cleanup.js` first (clean DB)
###   2. Run Section 1 → 2 → 3 → 4
###   3. Section 5 (Redirect) — uses URLs from Section 3
###   4. Section 6 (Analytics) — needs clicks from Section 5
###   5. Section 7 (Delete owned) — MUST come last before logout
###   6. Section 8 (Logout) — invalidates tokens
###
### ⚠️ KEY INSIGHT:
###   Section 5 uses {{anonCreate.response.body...}} and 
###   {{expCreate.response.body...}} — dynamic references
###   So the redirect URLs are always LIVE, never stale.
###
### 🔁 TO RE-RUN:
###   `node cleanup.js` then `Ctrl+Alt+R` (or run in order manually)
###